 dwr2560@zeus.tamu.edu (RING, DAVID WAYNE) writes:
> Well, I've patched nethack.exe so that it has my username at location 1041.
> And I tried the above, but it doesn't seem to do anything. If it helps, I'm
> on a VAX.

     There is more than one operating system which runs on a VAX.  Filename
"nethack.exe" suggests that you are running VMS.  If that's the case, any
mixed- or upper-case command line options must be enclosed in double quotes
because the C run-time library converts unquoted text into lower-case (after
the DCL command interpretor has just converted such text into upper-case).
Use "-D" rather than just -D.

