      You're right about not needing "-u wizard", but both the Unix and VMS
ports use the ASCII username, not a numeric ID code, compiled into the game
as WIZARD.  As long as the new username is the same length as the old one,
or shorter and he appended a trailing 0 byte, then what he did should be OK.
If the new username is longer then something will end up clobbered...


